(VAL-13: an in-place retype of a `value` holding text that is not a number
 raises the error flag so `On error` catches it, and the value keeps its
 text and its text tag. A text that is a number still converts.
 Up to 0.4.15 the failed retype left the value as 0 (this probe printed
 `cast failed` then `0`); vox main dfdfc7f states and does the new rule.
 Ran on vox main dfdfc7f: vox VAL-13.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   cast failed
   abc
   Text (dynamic)
   358
)
a value called bad is "abc".
bad is a number.
on error print "cast failed".
print bad.
print bad's type.
a value called good is "357".
good is a number.
print good add 1.
